itical and cultural history of France since its origins in the 12th century. Originally a hunting lodge for King Louis VII, it was transformed into a grand palace under the reign of Francis I beginning in 1528, attracting prominent artists and architects, including Rosso Fiorentino and Francesco Primaticcio. This transformation marked a significant shift in French royal residence and court life, establishing Fontainebleau as a center of artistic innovation and power.

